/-!
# Proved model exclusions for the faithful exchanged image

These source-specialized exclusions retain the original constituent and its
actual H image. They need neither a moved-original-L premise nor a replacement
actor. They exclude the binary linear-three central quotients, the Mathieu
groups and M₂₂ central covers, PSL₄(2), PSL₅(2), the triple A₆ cover, and the
two-component tensor and orthogonal actions from G.9.3.

This module is not an exhaustive classification theorem. The remaining
small-module branches and their source catalogue assembly, as well as the
noncentral-kernel paired A₅ alternative, remain obligations of the exchanged
image owner. The geometric ComponentHypothesis is supplied separately.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith G.9.3 and G.11.6, printed pp.353--357,366.
-/
